    "body": "Thanks - the review found no problems with the code. The only thing in the way is a conflict with main in `crates/app/tests/mcp.rs`. PR #444 (MCP stdio hardening) added tests at the same spot, after `the_stdio_loop_answers_line_for_line`.\n\nThe fix is to keep both blocks: main's #444 tests, and your `write_bored_disc_stl` + `detect_holes_fills_a_drill_from_its_model_and_undo_empties_it`. Each function closes with `}` and a blank line goes between them. We did that locally and it passes: `mcp` 9/9, `detect_holes` 1/1, clippy clean.\n\nWe tried to push that merge to your branch, but GitHub refused: the fork reports no push access for maintainers, even though \"Allow edits by maintainers\" shows as on. Could you `git merge upstream/main` with that resolution and push? Or toggle \"Allow edits by maintainers\" off and on, and we'll push it for you.\n",
